@vvo any chance in the future that the hits widget will receive a header footer option?
Use case would be to include a link at the bottom of results, that you want to show ONLY if results.

Right now the hits container when it first gets results will remove any html set within the element, instead of appending/prepending it.

@Giovanni-Mattucci Best way to do that right no would be to:

``` js
var search = instantsearch...
var hideWhenNoHits = {
  render: function(params) {
    if (params.hits.length === 0) {
      // hide some div
    }
  }
};

search.addWidget(hideWhenNoHits);
```

@vvo awesome thanks for putting me in the right direction! Got it to work exactly as I wanted.

Just an update to your snippet there:

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch...
var hideWhenNoHits = {
  render: function(params) {
    if (params.results.hits.length === 0) {
      // hide some div
    }
  }
};
search.addWidget(hideWhenNoHits);
```

